     <property name="plainText">
      <string>This script uses two CSV files:
1. A Depth-Time-Cross-Section file created using “Group by Time.”
2. A CSV file containing the surface area at each depth (in km²). This second file can be obtained by using “Group by Time” for a single day and applying the “Sum” function. The selected day must be repeated to create a subset of type 4.1. For a geographic coordinate system, the expression in the Calculate tool    should be:`*0 + ds2.km2`. For a rectangular coordinate system, use:
`*0 + cell_size_in_km2`

The result is a time series (CSV) showing the average value for a specified water volume for each year or month, taking into account variable depth intervals and varying depths in water body.

</string>
     </property>
